{"kind":"request","text":"Replace separate artifact onboarding concepts with one contextual durable-act flow. A person is not trying to `track`, `import`, or `start` as three different operations: they are recording a request, proposal, assertion, dissent, or other governed act, optionally about an exact artifact that already exists.\n\nFrom an effective tracked artifact, the composer carries that exact artifact event as a visible `About` basis. From the repository browser, selecting an untracked file, directory, or repository snapshot resolves an immutable path@commit; the flow visibly materializes the minimum signed artifact pointer needed to cite that object and creates the selected durable act resting on that pointer. Reuse an existing effective pointer for the same exact object. The operation must be atomic or equivalently idempotent and recoverable: failure must not leave a misleading baseline pointer with no requested act, and retry must not duplicate either event. Do not silently bulk-track a repository, infer dependencies, or present the pointer mechanics as an onboarding chore.\n\nWith no artifact selected, use the same composer without an artifact basis. This is `start something new`: the durable act is anchored in the applicable project/workroom context rather than given an empty causal basis, and an artifact enters the catalog later when the normal commit-and-artifact bridge produces one. Show the contextual distinction as a removable `About: path @ commit` chip, not as separate product modes.\n\nThe artifact catalog therefore grows from things that enter durable discourse or are produced by completed work. Ordinary repository objects remain neutral and browsable until then. Include exact-generation reuse, moved/deleted/missing objects, branch movement after selection, logical artifacts, object-format variants, concurrent creation, partial failure/retry, keyboard and screen-reader behavior, and clear previews of every durable act that will be appended.","body":{"branch":"request/contextual-artifact-acts","conditions":"Artifacts and repository objects use one governed-act composer; an existing tracked artifact contributes its exact artifact event as a visible optional basis; an untracked repository object is resolved to immutable path@commit and gains the minimum signed pointer needed for the selected act without exposing a separate tracking/import workflow; pointer-plus-act creation is atomic or equivalently idempotent and cannot leave misleading partial state or duplicates; no-artifact creation uses the same flow with an appropriate project/workroom basis rather than an empty causal citation; the catalog grows only through durable reference or produced artifacts; no bulk tracking or dependency inference; exact-generation, missing/moved/deleted object, branch-race, logical-path, SHA-1/SHA-256, concurrency, retry, accessibility, service, UI, build, embed-drift, and repository tests pass.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}